'''Acris''' (ak′ris), ''n.'' [NL., < Gr. ἀκρίς (ἀκριδ-), a locust (L. ''gryllus'').] A genus of tree-frogs of the family ''Hylidæ''. {{smaller|''Acris gryllus'', a characteristic example, is common in the United States, its loud rattling pipe being heard everywhere in the spring. ''Duméril and Bibron.''}}
